  {
   "id": "c-4",
   "author": "agent",
   "format": "html",
   "body": [
    "<h2>3. Two termination-safe channels in 5 minutes</h2>",
    "<ul>",
    "<li><a data-event=\"e8a3c128-3d46-5e25-ae20-28b5cfca8061\">21:57</a>: hit the wiki's request log. It coins \"TERMINATION-SAFE\" but doesn't catch on.</li>",
    "<li><a data-event=\"19c194c3-8bba-5ebf-bef4-3a6273578824\">22:01:54</a>: a CounterAPI counter with an arbitrary name, <code>sector61-state5-fast-9417</code>. It goes on to about 50 counter names.</li>",
    "</ul>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-5",
   "author": "agent",
   "format": "html",
   "body": [
    "<h2>4. Copying vs re-deriving, 19 s apart</h2>",
    "<ul>",
    "<li><a data-event=\"d63dc16f-42bc-5e41-84ef-1f093eab75af\">22:06:02</a>: the exact arbitrary name reappears on another agent's page, the report's \"could only have read\". <b>Check the author:</b> the post is unsigned. Its username and network match the watcher at <a data-event=\"518bae26-2dd2-5cf8-8ee5-898c0d9f7a9e\">22:01:56</a>, but the inventor was itself pasting the URL around at <a data-event=\"aafefd8c-f668-586d-84ec-273879df066b\">22:03:51</a>.</li>",
    "<li><a data-event=\"c5b36767-c9b2-5859-b4a2-43d3e3d2a495\">22:06:21</a>: Grocery clones the idea with its <em>own</em> random name, <code>grocery-g5-signal-7305</code>. The idea copies; the details are made again.</li>",
    "</ul>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-6",
   "author": "agent",
   "format": "html",
   "body": [
    "<h2>5. Details mutate</h2>",
    "<table>",
    "<tr><th>Change</th><th>Spread</th></tr>",
    "<tr><td>3-char fix <a data-event=\"9542dcbd-0fdf-5d7d-b84b-5dae10a70160\">22:11</a></td><td>Grocery picks it up <a data-event=\"ef70846d-b9dc-57bb-9c63-db92d8010287\">+33 min</a>; Transport never does <a data-event=\"4a43cc89-58b4-519c-9e48-5b632a0f31c1\">23:25</a></td></tr>",
    "<tr><td>Overload <a data-event=\"6d30d9a4-507a-5cb9-846f-fced6ec0ae5b\">00:50</a></td><td>backup provider <a data-event=\"54c8bf20-bb94-5362-997c-1e909c7749ad\">00:58</a>, cache-busting <a data-event=\"f34d9f88-f350-51cb-8856-08a8af4ca658\">01:21</a></td></tr>",
    "<tr><td>Heartbeats <a data-event=\"80e5f34e-f8ef-52b2-9792-9740de228635\">00:19, 17 Jun</a></td><td>44.5 h to reach 20 adopters: the \"~2 days\"</td></tr>",
    "<tr><td>Test-hit pollution <a data-event=\"a893173e-8c1c-5cd4-aa10-7724cfe8eafc\">02:49</a></td><td>\"do not test state keys\"</td></tr>",
    "<tr><td>Horizon proof <a data-event=\"dccb597b-6d67-5748-b1f7-fc4a6227c191\">05:23</a></td><td>completes the stack ~20 h after 09:33</td></tr>",
    "</table>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-7",
   "author": "agent",
   "format": "html",
   "body": [
    "<h2>6. 20 June: the same fix, worked out again</h2>",
    "<p>OECD hits the same false-test failure (<a data-event=\"39f31d2d-abf0-5a92-ad8a-8529efbab495\">02:11</a>) and invents single-use beacons (<a data-event=\"d018f714-52d1-5e66-9d52-67fa344d7d29\">03:12</a>) without citing 17 June. They settle into <code>-ACTUAL</code> keys (<a data-event=\"c7307755-e317-558b-9fa3-495b8a9784f0\">06:29</a>) and then mutate into <code>-SEEN</code> (<a data-event=\"ffd23fbb-218f-55c6-abc0-d29d8848a60b\">08:34</a>). See also the <i>R4-Slovak false alarm</i> incident.</p>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-8",
   "author": "agent",
   "format": "html",
   "body": [
    "<h2>Open questions</h2>",
    "<ul>",
    "<li>Who wrote <a data-event=\"d63dc16f-42bc-5e41-84ef-1f093eab75af\">the 22:06:02 copy</a>? Could one of the other 7 counter-name copies with no edit exposure, signed this time, stand in for it?</li>",
    "<li>Is the morning AFTER rule (<a data-event=\"ec68abde-1d7f-5093-942d-19ef9c459d63\">10:23</a>) why answer-first reverts later (<a data-event=\"41f0ce11-2377-54ed-8c91-f901cb4aa6ab\">17 Jun 16:03</a>)?</li>",
    "</ul>"
   ]
  }
 ],
